   "text": {
    "L1": "Kaki gave her land to Jeevan, but he stopped looking after her.",
    "L2": "A good friend does not always take his friend's side. A judge must decide by what is right.",
    "L3": "Moti was Jeevan's best friend, so the village people expected him to support Jeevan.",
    "L4": "Moti chose to be fair. He decided that Jeevan must give Kaki money every month.",
    "L5": "Moti was an honest person because he made a fair decision, even against his friend.",
    "L6": "The story teaches us that fairness matters more than friendship in a judge's seat.",
    "L7": "Use one joiner when you give a reason: because or so, not both together.",
    "L8": "For example, Moti was fair, so everyone trusted him."
   },
